{"call":330,"start_ns":552465334979212,"elapsed_ns":2803799,"ok":true,"source":"set_option maxHeartbeats 0\n\nopen BigOperators Real Nat Topology Rat\n\n/- If $x^2+y^2+z^2=49$ and $x+y+z=x^3+y^3+z^3=7$ , find $xyz$ . -/\ntheorem lean_workbook_21305 (x y z : ℝ) (h₁ : x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = 49) (h₂ : x + y + z = 7) (h₃ : x^3 + y^3 + z^3 = 7) : x*y*z = -112  := by\n  /-\n  Given \\( x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = 49 \\) and \\( x + y + z = 7 \\), we need to find \\( xyz \\).\n  1. Start by expressing \\( x^2 + y^2 + z^2 \\) in terms of \\( (x + y + z)^2 \\) and \\( 2(xy + yz + zx) \\):\n     \\[\n     x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = (x + y + z)^2 - 2(xy + yz + zx)\n     \\]\n     Substituting the known values:\n     \\[\n     49 = 7^2 - 2(xy + yz + zx)\n     \\]\n     Solving for \\( xy + yz + zx \\):\n     \\[\n     49 = 49 - 2(xy + yz + zx) \\implies 2(xy + yz + zx) = 0 \\implies xy + yz + zx = 0\n     \\]\n  2. Use the identity for the sum of cubes:\n     \\[\n     x^3 + y^3 + z^3 = (x + y + z)(x^2 + y^2 + z^2 - (xy + yz + zx)) + 3xyz\n     \\]\n     Substituting the known values:\n     \\[\n     7 = 7(49 - 0) + 3xyz \\implies 7 = 7 \\cdot 49 + 3xyz \\implies 7 = 343 + 3xyz\n     \\]\n     Solving for \\( xyz \\):\n     \\[\n     7 = 343 + 3xyz \\implies 3xyz = -336 \\implies xyz = -\\frac{336}{3} = -112\n     \\]\n  -/\n  -- Express x^2 + y^2 + z^2 in terms of (x + y + z)^2 and 2(xy + yz + zx)\n  have h₄ : x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = (x + y + z)^2 - 2 * (x * y + y * z + z * x) := by\n    nlinarith [sq_nonneg (x - y), sq_nonneg (y - z), sq_nonneg (z - x)]\n  -- Simplify using the known values\n  simp_all only [sq, add_assoc]\n  -- Use the identity for the sum of cubes and solve for xyz\n  nlinarith [sq_nonneg (x - y), sq_nonneg (y - z), sq_nonneg (z - x)]","lp":{"maxVar":58,"hyps":[["lt",[[0,-1]]],["le",[[3,-1],[2,2],[1,-1]]],["le",[[5,2],[4,-1],[3,-1]]],["le",[[6,2],[4,-1],[1,-1]]],["le",[[6,-2],[5,-2],[4,-1],[3,-1],[2,-2],[1,-1]]],["le",[[1,-1]]],["le",[[4,-1]]],["le",[[3,-1]]],["eq",[[4,-1],[3,-1],[1,-1]